&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the Senior Director, Commercial Legal and will be based in London with a 3 day/week in-office requirement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary Legal point of contact for go‑to‑market and procurement deals across EMEA, providing clear, practical advice to relevant teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage and negotiate a variety of commercial agreements, including customer, vendor, partnership, and reseller agreements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with cross‑functional teams to design and improve scalable contracting processes, playbooks, and tools that increase deal velocity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, maintain, and iterate on agreement templates, playbooks, and fallback positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in and advise on Vercel regional expansion strategies in EMEA and beyond&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI tools to build and refine workflows and processes that help the team work more efficiently and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to other Legal work as needed, which may include supporting commercial deals in APAC and AMER, or product, privacy, or security initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualified and in good standing in England and Wales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of legal experience, including 5+ years of in‑house commercial experience at a technology company (ideally AI, SaaS, PaaS, or IaaS)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deeply familiar with GDPR and related privacy regulations and able to confidently discuss privacy issues with customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of AI and cloud‑based services and the associated global regulatory landscape, with a willingness to dig deep into Vercel’s evolving product offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated skill and experience with using AI to build tools, workflows, and processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent judgment, with strong risk‑assessment and mitigation skills and the ability to make pragmatic recommendations with imperfect information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear and concise communicator, able to explain complex issues in plain language to a wide range of stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to confidently and independently negotiate technology agreements with enterprise customers and technology vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prioritization and organization skills, with the ability to manage a high volume of fast‑moving workstreams and diverse stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of building new or meaningfully improving existing programs or processes in a fast‑paced, high‑growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and low‑ego team member, willing to roll up your sleeves and take on work of varying scope and visibility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive in a fast-paced environment with a proven track record of building new or improving existing programs or processes at other high-growth companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Bonus if you have:&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Used Vercel’s products and services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting channel and reseller partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in other languages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
